{
  "description": "An architecture-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures recommender behavior through a stable DiagnosisProbe interface and turns measured results into an interpretation prompt.",
  "motivation": "Keep diagnosis compatible with model changes while grounding proposed improvements in observed training behavior and the shared macro-average validation HR@10 objective.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics alongside explicit metric_definitions, including measurement scope and limitations. Access the trained network through view.model and adapt feature, embedding, and scoring probes to its architecture. Training batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B × L; exclude padding from measurements. Use only public interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Mark unavailable attributes and simulator diversity/conformity traits as unobserved. Preserve all four dataset routes and generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category. Select models using the pinned macro validation HR@10; diagnostic proxies must not replace it. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], artifacts within the trial directory, and predictor generation synchronized with architecture changes.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        set view.model to evaluation mode\n        under no_grad:\n            inspect valid sequence positions and architecture-compatible scores\n            compute supported diagnostic measurements\n            record definitions, sample counts, and unavailable measurements\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics, metric_definitions}\n\ndef diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    format measured metrics with their definitions and limitations\n    request evidence-grounded interpretations and testable improvements\n    explicitly identify unobserved attributes\n    return prompt",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines a stable diagnostic contract with architecture-aware probes and grounded interpretation.",
    "negative": "Primarily an integration specification; no new diagnostic algorithm or empirical novelty is established."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support repeatable diagnosis and targeted model revisions across architectures.",
    "negative": "Benefits depend on probe quality and whether suggested changes improve independent validation HR@10."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces and batch structure are explicit.",
    "negative": "Architecture adaptation, correct masking, full-catalog scoring, and predictor consistency require care."
  }
}
